# Database Query Patterns

## Query Execution Standards

### Always Use Helper Functions
Use the established helper functions from [server/routes/optimizedRoutes.js](mdc:server/routes/optimizedRoutes.js):

- `executeCrudOperation()` for standard CRUD operations
- `executeRoundCrudOperation()` for rounds with slug generation
- `executeQuery()` for direct database queries

### Performance Timing
Always measure query performance:

```javascript
const startTime = startTiming();
const result = await executeQuery(query, params);
const duration = endTiming(startTime);

logger.info('Query completed', {
  duration: `${Math.round(duration)}ms`,
  queryType: 'OPERATION_TYPE'
});
```

## Query Optimization Patterns

### JOIN Queries for Performance
Use optimized service methods for complex queries:

```javascript
// GOOD - Use optimized service methods
const participants = await optimizedQueryService.getParticipantsWithStats();
const rounds = await optimizedQueryService.getRoundsWithDetails();
const news = await optimizedQueryService.getNewsWithAuthorAndStats();
```

### Parameterized Queries
Always use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection:

```javascript
// GOOD
const result = await executeQuery(
  'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1 AND status = $2',
  [userId, status]
);

// BAD - Never use string concatenation
const result = await executeQuery(
  `SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`
);
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Database Error Handling
```javascript
try {
  const result = await executeQuery(query, params);
  
  if (result.rows.length === 0) {
    return sendNotFoundResponse(res, 'Entity');
  }
  
  sendSuccessResponse(res, result.rows[0], 'QUERY_TYPE', duration);
} catch (error) {
  sendErrorResponse(res, error, 'Failed to execute query');
}
```

### Connection Health Checks
Use `checkDatabaseHealth()` for health endpoints:

```javascript
router.get('/health', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const dbHealth = await checkDatabaseHealth();
    res.json({ 
      status: 'OK', 
      database: dbHealth.status,
      pool: dbHealth.pool
    });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ status: 'ERROR' });
  }
});
```

## Cache Management

### Cache Invalidation
Always clear cache after data modifications:

```javascript
// After successful CRUD operations
notifyDataUpdate(entityType); // This handles cache clearing and WebSocket updates
```

### Cache Statistics
Use `optimizedQueryService.getCacheStats()` for monitoring:

```javascript
const stats = optimizedQueryService.getCacheStats();
```

## Data Validation Patterns

### Input Validation
Always validate input parameters:

```javascript
// Validate required fields
if (!title || !content) {
  return sendErrorResponse(res, new Error('Missing required fields'), 'Title and content are required', 400);
}

// Validate data types
if (typeof id !== 'string' || isNaN(parseInt(id))) {
  return sendErrorResponse(res, new Error('Invalid ID'), 'Invalid ID format', 400);
}
```

### Data Normalization
Use schema-based normalization for complex data:

```javascript
const normalizedData = normalizeData(req.body, {
  tags: { type: 'json', fallback: [] },
  metadata: { type: 'json', fallback: {} },
  status: { type: 'string', fallback: 'DRAFT' },
  order: { type: 'int', fallback: 0 }
});
```

## Specialized Query Patterns

### Slug Generation for Rounds
Use the specialized round CRUD operation for automatic slug generation:

```javascript
await executeRoundCrudOperation(
  'create',
  'INSERT INTO rounds (title, slug, ...) VALUES ($1, $2, ...) RETURNING *',
  [title, slug, ...],
  'round',
  'CREATE_ROUND',
  res,
  { title, slug } // Enables automatic slug generation
);
```

### Instagram URL Normalization
Use the helper function for Instagram URLs:

```javascript
const instagramUrl = normalizeInstagram(req.body.instagram);
// Handles: @username, username, https://instagram.com/username
// Returns: https://instagram.com/username
```

